#  Two-phase coexistence melting, with a gate at every stage.
#
#  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS.  A general-purpose toolkit ran this measurement for
#  tantalum and returned 3438 K.  The number is void: the cell contained no
#  solid at any point.  Its template creates velocities at TWICE the target
#  temperature over the whole cell, which melts everything before the
#  two-phase construction begins, and its solid-temperature diagnostic cannot
#  see that because the group it measures is fixed by INITIAL POSITION rather
#  than by structure - two halves of a uniform liquid report two temperatures
#  that differ only by noise, which is also what a real coexistence shows.
#  A temperature cannot tell you a phase.  Every stage below writes a dump,
#  and phase_gate.py reads the structure factor of each half:
#
#      python phase_gate.py *.dump --halves --data perfect.data --a 3.3052
#
#  Two differences from that template, both of them measured rather than
#  assumed:
#
#  1) The solid is built FAR BELOW the melting point (1200 K) and only the
#     liquid half is then heated.  Equilibrating the whole cell at the trial
#     temperature puts the crystal at its stability limit, where it melts at
#     random: 2400 K melted and 2600 K did not, which is noise, not physics.
#
#  2) Stage C2 brings BOTH halves to the trial temperature before the NPH
#     stage.  Without it the solid half keeps its 1200 K velocities (it has no
#     integrator in B and C) and NPH starts with a cold solid against a hot
#     liquid; the energy imbalance melts everything and the run measures the
#     setup rather than the melting point.  The apparent recrystallisation in
#     stage C is templating off that frozen wall, and is not evidence either.
#
#  Every melt stage is barostatted at zero pressure.  Melting half a cell at
#  6000 K in NVT drives the pressure up and destroys the solid by compression:
#  at 1600 K everything melted, which was a statement about the setup.
#
#  RUN, with the defaults below overridable from the command line:
#
#      lmp -in in.coexistence -var TTRY 2400
#      lmp -in in.coexistence -var TTRY 2400 -var POT potentials/W_taper.ugur \
#          -var EL W -var A0 3.1652 -var MASS 183.84
#
#  The temperature the NPH stage settles at is NOT the answer on its own -
#  read the phase of each half first.  in.coexistence_bracket is the cheaper
#  measurement and the one that stands: it needs no NPH stage and no
#  temperature reading at all.

variable TTRY  index 2400                             # trial temperature, K
variable POT   index potentials/Ta_force_taper.ugur   # potential file
variable EL    index Ta                               # element in that file
variable A0    index 3.3052                           # lattice constant, A
variable MASS  index 180.948                          # atomic mass
variable NX    index 6                                # cells across
variable NZ    index 30                               # cells along z, the long axis
variable TCOLD index 1200                             # where the solid is built
variable THOT  index 6000                             # where the liquid half is melted
variable NEQ   index 20000                            # steps per stage
variable NPH   index 120000                           # steps of coexistence

units metal
boundary p p p
atom_style atomic

lattice bcc ${A0}
region cell block 0 ${NX} 0 ${NX} 0 ${NZ}
create_box 1 cell
create_atoms 1 box
mass * ${MASS}

pair_style ugur
pair_coeff * * ${POT} ${EL}
neighbor 2.0 bin
timestep 0.002

#  the control the gate needs: a perfect crystal must return S = 1.000
write_data perfect.data nocoeff

variable lz equal "lz"
variable zc equal ${lz}/2
region rliq block INF INF INF INF INF ${zc} units box
group liq region rliq
group sol subtract all liq
compute Tliq liq temp
compute Tsol sol temp

thermo 2500
thermo_style custom step temp pe press vol c_Tliq c_Tsol

#  --- A: the whole cell SOLID, far below the melting point ---------------
velocity all create ${TCOLD} 4928459 mom yes rot yes dist gaussian
fix 1 all npt temp ${TCOLD} ${TCOLD} 0.1 iso 0 0 1.0
run ${NEQ}
unfix 1
write_dump all custom A_solid.dump id type x y z

#  --- B: melt the liquid half only; the solid half is not integrated ------
fix 1 liq nvt temp ${THOT} ${THOT} 0.1
run ${NEQ}
unfix 1
write_dump all custom B_halfmelt.dump id type x y z

#  --- C: bring the liquid half to the trial temperature ------------------
fix 1 liq nvt temp ${TTRY} ${TTRY} 0.1
run ${NEQ}
unfix 1
write_dump all custom C_cooled.dump id type x y z

#  --- C2: bring BOTH halves to it - see note (2) above -------------------
fix 1 all nvt temp ${TTRY} ${TTRY} 0.1
run ${NEQ}
unfix 1
write_dump all custom C2_both.dump id type x y z

#  --- D: the whole system under NPH; the interface pulls the temperature --
#  toward Tm through the latent heat.  Gate D_final before reading it.
reset_timestep 0
fix 1 all nph iso 0.0 0.0 0.5
run ${NPH}
write_dump all custom D_final.dump id type x y z
